From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ggml): GGML_OP_COUNT is 103, not 102

The kvmem patch inserts GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET_RECORD into ggml-ops. The prism
branch already carried GGML_OP_TURBO_WHT, so the enum lands on 103 rather than
the 102 the patch expected. Both static_asserts in ggml.c were left at the
pre-patch value; GGML_OP_NAME and GGML_OP_SYMBOL already have 103 entries, so
only the assertions needed bumping.

Note: ggml/include/ggml-rpc.h still asserts 101 and is stale independently of
this change (it was already stale at 102). Left alone because touching it means
deciding an RPC_PROTO_PATCH_VERSION bump.
---
 ggml/src/ggml.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml.c b/ggml/src/ggml.c
index 5aae92a..b86f218 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml.c
@@ -1134,7 +1134,7 @@ static const char * GGML_OP_NAME[GGML_OP_COUNT] = {
     "GATED_DELTA_NET_RECORD",
 };
 
-static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 102, "GGML_OP_COUNT != 102");
+static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 103, "GGML_OP_COUNT != 103");
 
 // ggml_turbo_wht
 
@@ -1282,7 +1282,7 @@ static const char * GGML_OP_SYMBOL[GGML_OP_COUNT] = {
     "gated_delta_net_record(q, k, v, g, beta, s)",
 };
 
-static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 102, "GGML_OP_COUNT != 102");
+static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 103, "GGML_OP_COUNT != 103");
 
 static_assert(GGML_OP_POOL_COUNT == 2, "GGML_OP_POOL_COUNT != 2");
 
